<header class="entry__head">
  <p class="kicker">The whole library</p>
  <h1 class="entry__title">Map of the collection</h1>
  <p class="entry__dek">Every entry, joined to the entries it cites and to its subjects. Drag to move, scroll to zoom, select a node to open it.</p>
</header>

{% if not collections.notes.length %}
<p class="empty-note">Nothing to map yet: the map fills in as entries are added and cite one another.</p>
{% else %}
<figure class="map">
  <canvas class="graph-canvas" data-graph="global" role="img" aria-label="Graph of every entry and subject in the library"></canvas>
  <figcaption><span class="fig-label">Key.</span> Filled circles are entries, sized by how many links they carry; hollow circles are subjects. The same catalogue, as a <a href="/notes/">list</a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endif %}
